  "authoringNote": "The final order f26f-order v1 states order date 2026-09-04 and no order time, so no instant is stated and no zone is inferred. Under C06 the date spans from 2026-09-03T10:00:00Z to 2026-09-05T12:00:00Z, both ends included. The single receipt f26f-receipt v1 references that exact order version and states receivedAt 2026-09-05T12:00:00Z, exactly the inclusive end of the span, which is not after the end. A receipt within the span when the order states no timestamp is not sequenced. The receipt is current, usable and linked, so R05 is manual_review for the administrative reviewer with only R05.receipt_unsequenced, naming [f26f-order v1, f26f-receipt v1] in canonical order. It is neither before the start of the span (no R05.receipt_before_order) nor after its end (it does not follow the order). No receipt candidate, R05.order_receipt_missing or absence condition holds. R05 cites the receipt order document ID, order version and receivedAt and the order date (four). R04 passes citing the encounter status, date and practitioner identifier and the order status, date and practitioner identifier (six; the null completion and order times supply no fact). R02 passes citing the beneficiary name and identifier of the encounter, the order and the receipt (six). The rest follows the supported packet, checked by hand: the final encounter (2026-08-26) and the final signed order (2026-09-04) both name practitioner identifier SYN-PRAC-0001; the order is after the encounter, on a different date, and within the inclusive C01 bound 2027-02-26; the order item code K0823 equals the case; the named supplier record f26f-supplier-status v1 is usable and states non_exempt, established, no new enrollment, no ownership change and the interval 2026-01-01 to 2026-12-31, which contains the assessment date 2026-10-18. R01 passes citing the seven supplier record facts and the order item code; R03 passes citing the nine order facts. R06 stays manual_review for the qualified clinical reviewer with R06.clinical_review and the five full /clinical/ pointers; it neither blocks nor satisfies readiness and draws no medical necessity conclusion. R07 passes citing the stated LCMP flag false (the null evaluation date supplies no fact); no ATP, specialty, home assessment or proof-of-delivery item is required. R08 passes on the reviewed pack and the supported date. R10 is not_applicable with R10.pure_assessment. clinicalReviewRequired is true. R09 passes. The state is needs_human_review from R05 alone. Quarantine and superseded lists are empty, and every parent affectedDocuments set is empty: the order and receipt are named only at condition level (C07).",
